  "description": "This habitat Garden has been designed to bring together native bushland character, wild meadow softness, and selective productive planting. We have created a habitat-rich, low-chemical landscape that supports pollinators, small birds, butterflies, and local insect life while providing a calming daily outlook from the home. The planting palette prioritises Victorian natives, favouring species indigenous to the Surrey Hills area and has been selected for year-round flowering, seasonal movement, and layered ecological function. This forward-thinking design focuses on long-term resilience, sensory experience and supporting the re-establishment of local biodiversity.",
